WHAT: two ways a caller can point the server at an arbitrary directory:
(a) `PipelineService.save_plan` (pipeline/service.py) accepts a model-authored `repo_root` and a `workspace` argument, both server paths. A remote principal must use `repo_url` instead (wired by a later story).
(b) `pipeline/workspace.py` `validate_workspace` (used by save_plan, decompose_plan and the dashboard's decompose route) checks only a sensitive-location deny list, so any git repo on the server is accepted. `check_repo_root_allowed` (same module) enforces the opt-in `PIPELINE_ALLOWED_REPO_ROOTS` allowlist but is only called for the plan's own repo_root.

