WHAT: new module `pipeline/repo_clone.py`, no callers yet (SA-05 wires it). A standalone server clones each plan's repository into its own volume instead of reading a host directory.

API:
- `parse_repo_url(url: str, environ=None) -> tuple[str, str, str]` returning (host, owner, repo) or raising `RepoUrlError(ValueError)`. Rules: scheme `https` only; host (lower-cased) must be in `PIPELINE_REPO_URL_HOSTS` (comma-separated, default `github.com`); no userinfo (`user@`, `user:pass@`), no port other than none/443, no query or fragment; path must be exactly `/<owner>/<repo>` or `/<owner>/<repo>.git` where owner and repo match `[A-Za-z0-9._-]+`, are not `.` or `..`, and repo has any trailing `.git` stripped. Test-only allowance: when `PIPELINE_REPO_URL_ALLOW_FILE=1`, a `file:///abs/path/<owner>/<repo>.git` URL is accepted with host `local` (off by default; document it as test-only in the docstring).
- `managed_path(url, environ=None) -> Path`: `<PIPELINE_REPOS_ROOT>/<host>/<owner>/<repo>`; `PIPELINE_REPOS_ROOT` required (raise RepoUrlError naming the variable if unset). The resolved path must stay inside the resolved root (defence in depth).
- `ensure_clone(url, environ=None, timeout=600) -> Path`: if the managed path has a `.git`, run `git -C <path> fetch --prune origin`; otherwise `git clone --no-tags <url> <path>` (create parents 0o750). Use `subprocess.run([...], check=False, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)` with an argv list, never a shell. On failure raise `RepoCloneError(RuntimeError)` whose message names the operation and the URL with credentials stripped - never git's stderr verbatim (it can echo a token); log stderr's first line at WARN only after replacing any `https://<anything>@` with `https://***@`.
- Credentials: when `PIPELINE_GIT_TOKEN_FILE` is set, the token is read from that file (strip whitespace; refuse with RepoCloneError if the file is group/world readable, i.e. mode & 0o077) and supplied through `GIT_ASKPASS`: write a 0700 helper script to a private temp dir that prints the value of an env var `PIPELINE_GIT_ASKPASS_TOKEN`, set `GIT_ASKPASS=<script>`, `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, `PIPELINE_GIT_ASKPASS_TOKEN=<token>` only in the child env, and delete the temp dir afterwards. The token must never appear in argv, in `.git/config`, or in a log line. The https username is `x-access-token`: the askpass script prints `x-access-token` when its first argument contains "Username" and the token otherwise. Never put a username or token in the URL.

