- parse_repo_url rejects: http://, ssh://, git@host:o/r, a host not on the list, `https://user:pw@github.com/o/r`, `https://github.com/o/r?x=1`, `https://github.com/o/r#f`, `https://github.com/o`, `https://github.com/o/r/extra`, `https://github.com/../r`, `https://github.com:8443/o/r`, and file:// when the allowance is unset;
- parse_repo_url accepts `https://github.com/Org/Repo.git` -> ("github.com", "Org", "Repo") and honours a custom PIPELINE_REPO_URL_HOSTS;
- managed_path without PIPELINE_REPOS_ROOT raises RepoUrlError naming it;
- with PIPELINE_GIT_TOKEN_FILE at mode 0644 -> RepoCloneError; at 0600 the clone succeeds and the token string appears neither in the clone's .git/config nor in caplog text (use a fake token value);
- a clone failure (URL to a missing bare repo) raises RepoCloneError whose message does not contain the token.

