WHAT: a remote plan names `repo_url` (SA-03 refuses repo_root/workspace from remote callers). Wire `pipeline/repo_clone.py` (SA-04) so the server clones the repo and sets the plan's `repo_root` to the managed clone itself.

CHANGE:
- pipeline/remote_scope.py: add `resolve_repo_url(plan: dict) -> dict | None` - when the plan has `repo_url` and also `repo_root`, return an error dict `{"ok": False, "error": "a plan names repo_url or repo_root, not both"}`; when it has `repo_url` (must be a non-empty str, else error), call `repo_clone.ensure_clone(url)` and set `plan["repo_root"] = str(path)`; map `RepoUrlError`/`RepoCloneError` to `{"ok": False, "error": str(exc)}`; return None on success or when there is no repo_url.
- pipeline/service.py `save_plan`: after SA-03's remote check and before the workspace/allowlist block, call `resolve_repo_url(plan)` for ANY principal (local operators may use repo_url too) and return its error dict when not None. The existing `check_repo_root_allowed` then runs on the clone path, so a deployment that sets `PIPELINE_ALLOWED_REPO_ROOTS` to `PIPELINE_REPOS_ROOT` accepts it.
